From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:07:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/13] jm-v7 012: keep the emulated geometry shader across
 meta operations

On v6/v7 meta_gfx_start()/meta_gfx_end() did not save the bound geometry
shader. Binding a meta pipeline clears it (vk_meta binds every graphics
stage), so after a blit, clear or resolve inside a sequence of draws the
next draw ran without the application's geometry shader and without its
transform feedback capture. Save it, clear it and restore it as v9+ does
for gs/tcs/tes, and mark the GS state dirty both ways.

Found in review of 007-011. Build-tested only, no Bifrost device run.
biblioklept

Generated-by: LLM
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
